<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36176" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phthīa</span></b> , ae, f.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φθία</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city in Thessaliotis</i>, <i>the birthplace of Achilles</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 3,
			4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 1, 284</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phthīas</span></b> ,
				ădis, f., <i>a
				Phthian woman</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. H. 7, 165</span></i> (al.
			Phthia).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phthīōta</span></b> ,
				ae, and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phthī-ōtes</span></b> , ae,
				m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φθιώτης</span>, <i>a Phthiote</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Tusc.
				1, 10, 21</span></i>.—In plur., <i>the Phthiotes</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 7,
				14, § 28</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 33,
			32</span></i>; <i><span class="en">34</span></i>; <i><span class="en">36,
			15</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phthīōtis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φθιῶτις</span>, <i>Phthiotis</i>, <i>a district of Thessaly</i>, <i>in which Phthia lay</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 8,
				15, § 29</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 28,
			6</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>D.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phthī-ōtĭcus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φθιωτικός</span>, <i>of Phthiotis</i>, <i>Phthiotian</i>, <b>poet.</b> for
				<i>Thessalian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					33, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tempe,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					64, 35</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>E.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phthīus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Phthia</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vir,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Achilles</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Prop. 2, 13, 38</span></i>
			 (2, 5, 22); cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Achilles,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 4, 6, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rex,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Peleus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Am. 2, 17, 17</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
